### The Anemic Domain Model Anti-Pattern

An **Anemic Domain Model** is a class that holds data with getters and setters but contains **no business logic**. All business rules are implemented by external services that reach into the object:
```java
// Anemic Anti-Pattern: External code manipulates internals
order.setStatus("SHIPPED");
order.setShippedDate(new Date());
```

**The Rich Domain Solution (Domain Method):**
Instead of exposing raw setters, provide meaningful **Domain Method** actions that encapsulate business rules and perform complete atomic operations internally:
```java
// Rich Domain Action: Encapsulates state transition
order.ship(trackingNumber);
```

---

### Comparing Anemic vs Rich Domain Models in Code

```java
class BankCard {
    private String cardNumber;
    private boolean blocked;
    private int pinAttempts;

    public BankCard(String cardNumber) {
        this.cardNumber = cardNumber;
        this.blocked = false;
        this.pinAttempts = 0;
    }

    // Rich Domain Method: Encapsulates business rule internally
    public boolean verifyPin(int enteredPin, int correctPin) {
        if (blocked) {
            System.out.println("Card is blocked. Authentication rejected.");
            return false;
        }

        if (enteredPin == correctPin) {
            pinAttempts = 0; // Reset on success
            System.out.println("PIN verified successfully.");
            return true;
        } else {
            pinAttempts++;
            System.out.println("Invalid PIN. Attempt " + pinAttempts + " of 3.");
            if (pinAttempts >= 3) {
                blocked = true;
                System.out.println("Card has been blocked due to excessive invalid attempts.");
            }
            return false;
        }
    }
}

public class RichDomainDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        BankCard card = new BankCard("4111-2222-3333-4444");
        card.verifyPin(1111, 4321);
        card.verifyPin(2222, 4321);
        card.verifyPin(3333, 4321); // Third strike: blocks card automatically
    }
}
```

**Console Output:**
```text
Invalid PIN. Attempt 1 of 3.
Invalid PIN. Attempt 2 of 3.
Invalid PIN. Attempt 3 of 3.
Card has been blocked due to excessive invalid attempts.
```

---

### Architectural Value

Rich domain methods ensure business rules are enforced consistently, preventing calling code from bypassing critical logic.

